div><p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/nyc/">New York</a> / Vehicle lettering and focused graphics</p><p class="eyebrow">VISION GRAPHICS · NEW YORK</p><h1>Vehicle lettering and focused graphics</h1><p class="lead">Vehicle graphics do not have to cover every panel to communicate a business identity. A well-placed logo, short service description and clear contact route can give a work vehicle a coordinated appearance. For New York teams, that may be a useful starting point when vehicles vary in color or body style. Vision Graphics can help organize a repeatable graphic set around the space available, while accounting for panel shapes, existing markings and the condition of each vehicle before production is planned.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/nyc/contact/?product=Vehicle%20lettering%20and%20focused%20graphics">Discuss your project <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="#options">Explore options <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></div><figure class="project-image product-photo"><img src="/nyc/assets/mcs-new-service-vehicle-wraps-960.webp" srcset="/nyc/assets/mcs-new-service-vehicle-wraps-480.webp 480w, /nyc/assets/mcs-new-service-vehicle-wraps-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 50vw" alt="Signage example related to Vehicle lettering and focused graphics" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Illustrative sign example · Michigan Custom Signs source</figcaption></figure></section><section class="wrap section article-layout"><article><section><h2>Use the body color intentionally</h2><p>Separate letters and decals leave the vehicle visible, so contrast is essential. Review each design against the actual paint color and avoid small details that disappear from a distance. The rear may need a simpler arrangement than the sides because its usable space is different.</p></section><section><h2>Create a repeatable record</h2><p>Keep approved artwork, placement drawings and vehicle-specific dimensions together. This makes replacements and future additions easier to scope. Before each installation, confirm the actual vehicle, surface condition and any changes to the contact information or branding.</p></section><section id="options"><p class="eyebrow">MATERIALS &amp; APPROACHES</p><h2>Find the right fit.</h2><div class="options-grid"><div><h3>Cut lettering</h3><p>Apply names and short messages as separate characters.</p></div><div><h3>Printed logo decals</h3><p>Present full-color brand artwork within a defined graphic area.</p></div><div><h3>Coordinated vehicle kits</h3><p>Develop consistent elements that can be adapted to different body styles.</p></div></div></section><section><h2>Where it can work</h2><ul class="check-list"><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Single service vehicles</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Mixed company fleets</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Replacement logos and contact updates</li></ul></section><section class="faqs"><h2>A few useful answers.</h2><details><summary>Are graphics a lower-coverage alternative to a wrap?<span>+</span></summary><p>Yes. The design can focus on selected areas while using the existing vehicle color as the background.</p></details><details><summary>Can old lettering be covered?<span>+</span></summary><p>Existing graphics and adhesive should be assessed. Removal and surface preparation may be needed for a sound result.</p></details></section></article><aside class="product-aside"><p class="eyebrow">LET’S START WITH THE DETAILS</p><h3>Have a space in mind?</h3><p>A photo, a few measurements and your project ZIP help us ask the right questions.</p><a href="/nyc/contact/?photo=1" class="btn dark"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-camera" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.997 4a2 2 0 0 1 1.76 1.05l.486.9A2 2 0 0 0 18.003 7H20a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V9a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h1.997a2 2 0 0 0 1.759-1.048l.489-.904A2 2 0 0 1 10.004 4z"></path><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3"></circle></svg> Send a project photo</a><hr><h3>Related possibilities</h3><a href="/nyc/vehicle-wraps/">Vehicle wraps<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a href="/nyc/custom-decals/">Custom decals<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoi